   "reason": "Enemies rate an ally queen as highly as Rookie, so a Duchess normally dies in a turn; while Rookie is smoked the king cannot flee her threats and the summon's captures do NOT break the smoke (only Rookie's own do), so the queen can carve while Rookie stays invisible. | Magnet's grab lines are Rookie's current form's lines (magnetDirs reads state.form), so in bishop form she can drag a guard along a diagonal — a pull that is simply illegal in rook form.",
